            <ArticleTitle>Mycotic right coronary artery aneurysm: CT and MR diagnosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>667-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A clostridial mycotic aneurysm of the right coronary artery was diagnosed by the use of multiple imaging modalities including gated magnetic resonance imaging. Percutaneous drainage was performed as a palliative measure in hope of avoiding repeat sternotomy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
